{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117836","id":3446380271,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7Na5bv","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117836","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117836.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117836.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117836","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117836/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117836/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117836/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/46315bff9dca4dd47e579b3682c38277840eccea","number":117836,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Implement MeshRD for RenderingDevice buffers","user":{"login":"maidopi-usagi","id":33864304,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzODY0MzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33864304?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maidopi-usagi","html_url":"https://github.com/maidopi-usagi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maidopi-usagi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maidopi-usagi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maidopi-usagi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maidopi-usagi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maidopi-usagi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maidopi-usagi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maidopi-usagi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maidopi-usagi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maidopi-usagi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes (partially) https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/7209.\r\n\r\nThis PR adds `MeshRD`, a low-level `Mesh` resource for indirect procedural GPU meshes.\r\n\r\nThe basic idea is simple: users create the `RenderingDevice` buffers themselves, pass those RIDs to `MeshRD.add_surface()`, then fill the buffers from compute shaders. `MeshRD` makes the result usable as a normal `Mesh` resource, so it can be assigned to `MeshInstance3D.mesh`.\r\n\r\nThis avoids the GPU -> CPU -> GPU roundtrip that `ArrayMesh` requires, and keeps ownership clear: `MeshRD` does not allocate, own, free, expose, or serialize the buffers passed to it. The caller owns all RD buffers.\r\n\r\nSince https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118973 already exposes existing mesh surface RD buffer RIDs, this PR no longer tries to cover that use case. It only focuses on creating a mesh from caller-owned buffers and drawing it indirectly.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTested locally on macOS arm64.\r\n\r\nDemo project:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/maidopi-usagi/godot_meshrd_demo\r\n\r\nIncludes the following demos:\r\n\r\n<table> <tr> <td align=\"center\"> <img src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/64992f71-749f-40dd-a1bf-e4d2b97c6c56\" width=\"100%\" /> </td> <td align=\"center\"> <img src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/33173bd6-233d-40c2-bf73-d33a9a87a46e\" width=\"100%\" /> </td> <td align=\"center\"> <img src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7b10aa1d-0953-4b6b-8b1a-848efad25a5d\" width=\"100%\" /> </td> </tr> <tr> <td align=\"center\"><sub>Marching Cube Metaball</sub></td> <td align=\"center\"><sub>Procedural ClipMap Terrain</sub></td> <td align=\"center\"><sub>Animated Ribbons</sub></td> </tr> </table>\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### API Overview\r\n\r\n#### `MeshRD`\r\n\r\n| Method | Description |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `add_surface(format, primitive, vertex_count, vertex_buffer, aabb, attribute_buffer, index_count, index_buffer, ...)` | Attach caller-owned RD buffers as a mesh surface. |\r\n| `surface_set_indirect_buffer(surf_idx, indirect_buffer, offset)` | Set or replace the indirect draw buffer for a surface. |\r\n| `clear_surfaces()` / `surface_remove(surf_idx)` | Surface management. |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Minimal Usage\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar rd := RenderingServer.get_rendering_device()\r\n\r\nvar vb := rd.vertex_buffer_create(vertex_buffer_size, PackedByteArray(), RenderingDevice.BUFFER_CREATION_AS_STORAGE_BIT)\r\nvar ib := rd.index_buffer_create(max_indices, RenderingDevice.INDEX_BUFFER_FORMAT_UINT32, PackedByteArray(), false, RenderingDevice.BUFFER_CREATION_AS_STORAGE_BIT)\r\nvar ind := rd.storage_buffer_create(20, PackedByteArray(), RenderingDevice.STORAGE_BUFFER_USAGE_DISPATCH_INDIRECT)\r\n\r\nvar mesh_rd := MeshRD.new()\r\nmesh_rd.add_surface(\r\n    Mesh.ARRAY_FORMAT_VERTEX | Mesh.ARRAY_FORMAT_INDEX,\r\n    Mesh.PRIMITIVE_TRIANGLES,\r\n    max_vertices,\r\n    vb,\r\n    aabb,\r\n    RID(),\r\n    max_indices,\r\n    ib,\r\n    null,\r\n    Vector4(),\r\n    ind,\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\n_Disclaimer: AI was used to resolve the conflicts and update the example demo project. The core changes and documentations were written by hand._\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":